commit 2c1dd13d41586f63f40ba9ce45ce201026ab52b0
Author: Francisco D' Agostino <dagostinofrancisco@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Jul 10 19:44:56 2026 -0300

    ChatSession: cancel the generation task when the consumer goes away (#413)
    
    The generation task from generateTask() is unstructured, so cancelling
    streamMap's task (stream onTermination) never propagated to it. A caller
    that stops consuming mid-stream (barge-in) and immediately issues the
    next request deadlocks: 'await genTask.value' waits for the full
    generation while holding the session's serial cache lock. Cancel the
    generation task explicitly on consumer termination and on task
    cancellation; the generate loop already checks Task.isCancelled per
    token, so it stops promptly.

diff --git a/Libraries/MLXLMCommon/ChatSession.swift b/Libraries/MLXLMCommon/ChatSession.swift
index b135e79..f06b286 100644
--- a/Libraries/MLXLMCommon/ChatSession.swift
+++ b/Libraries/MLXLMCommon/ChatSession.swift
@@ -761,11 +761,24 @@ public final class ChatSession {
                                 pendingToolCalls.append(toolCall)
                             } else if let value = transform(item) {
                                 if case .terminated = continuation.yield(value) {
+                                    genTask.cancel()
                                     break
                                 }
                             }
                         }
 
+                        // The generation task is unstructured, so cancellation of
+                        // this task (stream onTermination) does not propagate to
+                        // it. Without an explicit cancel, `await genTask.value`
+                        // would wait for the FULL generation while holding the
+                        // cache lock — deadlocking the session's next call (e.g.
+                        // a caller that cancels mid-stream and immediately asks
+                        // again). The generate loop checks Task.isCancelled per
+                        // token, so this stops it promptly.
+                        if Task.isCancelled {
+                            genTask.cancel()
+                        }
+
                         // wait for the task to complete -- this is important in
                         // the case where we broke the loop early as the generation
                         // work may continue (briefly) and use the KVCache

