commit 4d73efe88aff34c6a86b7a6be8356ac22f915dd4
Author: GoodOlClint <goodolclint@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Jul 9 13:11:09 2026 -0500

    ci: pin swift-format version so lint doesn't drift across PRs (#386)
    
    The lint job resolved swift-format from `releases/latest`, so a new upstream
    release could silently change formatting rules. When 603.0.0 shipped, its
    OrderedImports rule started grouping attributed imports (@_spi/@testable) into
    a trailing block — reformatting MTPSpeculativeTokenIteratorTests.swift, a file
    no in-flight PR had touched. Because the lint step runs `pre-commit run --all`
    over the whole repo, this turned lint red on every open PR simultaneously,
    with a diff unrelated to any of them.
    
    Pin the version (603.0.0, what `latest` resolved to at pin time) so lint is
    reproducible and only changes when someone deliberately bumps it, and reformat
    the one drifted file to satisfy it.
    
    Note: the pre-commit hook is `language: system`, so contributors' local
    swift-format still isn't version-locked to CI; matching a pinned tool version
    locally is the reliable way to reproduce lint.

